+# Feature Specification: Fix order rule bugs
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-09 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Three weekly reports: lower-case SKU refused; no free shipping at exactly €50.00; VAT one cent low on some lines.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Lower-case product codes (P1)
+Sales staff key in codes as customers say them (`lb-220`).
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** product LB-220, **When** an order uses `lb-220` or ` lb-220 `, **Then** it is accepted as LB-220.
+
+### User Story 2 - Free shipping at exactly €50.00 (P1)
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** goods of €50.00 after discounts, **Then** shipping is €0.00.
+2. **Given** goods of €49.99, **Then** shipping is charged by weight band.
+
+### User Story 3 - VAT rounded half up per line (P2)
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** one item at €1.99, standard rate, **Then** line VAT is €0.44 (0.4378 → 0.44).
+2. **Given** a line whose VAT is exactly 0.5 cent, **Then** it rounds up.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: SKU lookup is case-insensitive and ignores surrounding spaces (README "Products").
+- **FR-002**: Shipping is free when goods are €50.00 (5000 cents) or more (README "Shipping").
+- **FR-003**: Line VAT is rounded half up to the cent (README "VAT", "Money").
+- Boundaries: 4999 / 5000 cents; exactly 0.5 cent of VAT.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All three reported cases give the documented result; existing tests still pass.
+
+## Assumptions
+- README is authoritative; no README change needed.
